                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Examples"} Examples
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#MonoidalStructure"} Monoidal structure
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em cyclotomic spectrum
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectrum"} equivariant spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            for all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+groups"} cyclic groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_p = \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow S^1
            inside the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi p
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^{C_p} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} E
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_P
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
            with the full object.
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-spectra" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"} topological Hochschild homology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi THH
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = THH(A)
            are naturally cyclotomic spectra, and this is where the concept originates: by the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi THH
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} THH(A)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-infinity+ring"} E-infinity ring
            of functions on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            are equivalent to plain loops.
          %p
            Cyclotomic structure is the origin of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclotomic+trace"} cyclotomic trace
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi THH
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi TC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} THH \longrightarrow TC
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"} topological Hochschild homology
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+cyclic+homology"} topological cyclic homology
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Throughout, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi p
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_p \subset S^1
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
            of order
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
          %p
            A definition says that a cyclotomic spectrum is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+equivariant+spectrum"} genuine equivariant spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (modeled on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Φ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi p
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^{C_p} X
            for all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi p
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_p \subset S^1
          %p
            A more abstract definition was given in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"} Nikolaus-Scholze 17
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          #CyclotomicSpectrumViaTateSpectra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em cyclotomic spectrum
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi Spectra
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B S^1 \to Spectra
                  which takes
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
                  unique point of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B S^1
                  to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  for each prime number
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  a homomorphism of spectra with such circle group action
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F_p \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow X^{t C_p}
                %p
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+spectrum"} Tate spectrum
                  (the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi cofib
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi norm
                              %mi p
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{t C_p} \coloneqq cofib( X_{C_p} \overset{norm_p}{\to} X^{C_p} )
                  of the
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+map"} norm map
                %p#CircleQuotient
                  where the circle action on the Tate spectrum comes from the canonical identification
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mi p
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1/C_p \simeq S^1
            %p
              (These morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p
              are called the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphisms"} Frobenius morphisms
              of the cyclotomic structure, due to
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Frobenius+morphism#EInfinityFrobenius"} this def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Frobenius+morphism#EInfinityFrobeniusReducesToOrdinaryFrobenius"} this example
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, def. 1.3, def. II.1.1
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a spectrum with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups"} stable homotopy groups
              bounded below, then def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclotomicSpectrumViaTateSpectra"}
              is equivaent to the traditional:
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CycSp
                      %mo −
                      %mi gen
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi CycSp
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CycSp_-^{gen} \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} CycSp_-
            %p
              from traditional (“genuine”) cyclotomic spectra bounded below to bounded below cyclotomic spectra in the sense of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclotomicSpectrumViaTateSpectra"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, prop. II.3.4, theorem II.6.9
            ).
          %h2#Examples Examples
          #THHCarriesCyclotomicStructure.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"}> topological Hochschild homology
                )
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+ring"} A-∞ ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"} topological Hochschild homology
              spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi THH
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} THH(A)
              naturally carries the structure of a cyclotomic spectrum (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclotomicSpectrumViaTateSpectra"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, section II.2, def. III.2.3
            )
          #TrivialCyclotomicSpectra.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong (trivial cyclotomic spectra)
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              becomes a cyclotomic spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi triv
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{triv}
              in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclotomicSpectrumViaTateSpectra"}
              by equipping it
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  with the trivial
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              %li
                %p
                  for each prime
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  with the composite morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mrow
                            %mi t
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f_p
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\mathbb{S}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathbb{S}^{C_p}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathbb{S}^{t C_p}
                %p
                  (the first being the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mi p
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊣
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi C
                                %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( B C_p \times (-) \dashv (-)^{C_p} )
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
                  into the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fixed+points"} homotopy fixed points
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+spectrum"} Tate spectrum
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-equivariant" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1/C_p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
                  between trivial action and homotopy fixed points by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                  morphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi t
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mi p
                            %mo )
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X \longrightarrow \left(X^{t C_p}\right)^{S^1/C_p}
                %p as the composite
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi X
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mi p
                            %mo )
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mo ⟶
                        %msup
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi t
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mi p
                            %mo )
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X \to X^{S^1}
                        \\simeq
                        \\left( X^{C_p} \right)^{S^1/C_p}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\left( X^{t C_p} \right)^{S^1/C_p}
                        \\,.
            %p
              This construction constitutes a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28infinity%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (infinity,1)-functor
              to taking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+cyclic+homology"} topological cyclic homology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CycSpectra
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi TC
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi triv
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CycSpectra
                    \\underoverset{\underset{TC}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{(-)^{triv}}{\longleftarrow}}{\bot}
                    Spectra
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, example II.1.2 (ii) and middle of p. 126
            )
          #CyclotomicSphereSpectrum.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong (cyclotomic sphere spectrum)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
              regarded as a cyclotomic spectrum via example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialCyclotomicSpectra"}
              is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em cyclotomic sphere spectrum
            %p
              As such it is equivalently its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"} topological Hochschild homology
              according to example
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#THHCarriesCyclotomicStructure"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi triv
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi THH
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{S}^{triv} \simeq THH(\mathbb{S})
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#NikolausScholze17"}> Nikolaus-Scholze 17, example II.1.2 (ii)
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#MonoidalStructure Monoidal structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (infinity,1)-category
            of cyclotomic spectra is the cyclotomic sphere spectrum from example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclotomicSphereSpectrum"}
            (
            %a{:href => "#BlumbergMandell13"}> Blumberg-Mandell 13, example 4.9
            )
